# Sources layer — primary statutes

`sources/` holds the raw, public-domain tax law material this product reasons from. Every rule in `knowledge/` cites back to a specific file here.

## Layout

```
sources/
├── india/
│   ├── ita-1961/
│   │   ├── _manifest.yaml
│   │   ├── s6-residence.pdf
│   │   ├── s6-residence.md
│   │   └── ...
│   ├── dtaa-india-us/
│   ├── cbdt-circulars/
│   └── black-money-act/
└── us/
    ├── irc/
    ├── irs-publications/
    └── treaty/
```

## `_manifest.yaml` format

One manifest per source directory, declaring the stable IDs used elsewhere in the repo.

```yaml
# sources/india/ita-1961/_manifest.yaml
documents:
  - id: IN-ITA-S6
    title: "Income Tax Act 1961 — Section 6, Residence in India"
    authority: "Government of India, Ministry of Finance"
    url_when_fetched: "https://incometaxindia.gov.in/..."
    as_of_date: "2026-04-01"
    files:
      pdf: "s6-residence.pdf"
      markdown: "s6-residence.md"

  - id: IN-ITA-S90
    title: "Income Tax Act 1961 — Section 90, Agreement with foreign countries"
    ...
```

## Naming convention

Stable IDs follow `<COUNTRY>-<CORPUS>-<LOCATOR>`:

- `IN-ITA-S6` — India, Income Tax Act, Section 6
- `IN-DTAA-ART-4` — India (treaty), DTAA with US, Article 4
- `IN-BMA-S43` — India, Black Money Act, Section 43
- `IN-CBDT-24-2022` — India, CBDT Circular 24/2022
- `US-IRC-7701B` — US, IRC, Section 7701(b)
- `US-PUB-519` — US, IRS Publication 519
- `US-TREATY-ART-13` — US (treaty), Article 13

Once assigned, a source ID never changes. If a document is superseded, add a new ID and mark the old one.

## Adding a new source

1. Download the PDF.
2. Run `pdftotext -layout` to extract markdown. Commit both.
3. Add the entry to `_manifest.yaml` with ID, title, authority, URL, as-of date.
4. Reference the new ID in any rule that needs it.

## Hard rules

1. **Do not fabricate a source.** If a rule you're authoring needs a statute that isn't downloaded, stop and flag it.
2. **Only public-domain government works.** Statutes, treaties, official publications. No commercial commentary.
3. **Do not edit the extracted markdown to clean up the text.** Keep it verbatim so citations remain verifiable.
